course: dictionary
lesson: 7667
title: Propeller: what it does
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A propeller is a set of blades that spin around. It pushes a boat, ship or aircraft forward. When you meet the word, look at the words around it to find its meaning.
explain: «A propeller's twisted blades push water backwards as they spin, so the ship moves forward.» The blades push the water back, and the water pushes the ship forward. That is why a boat moves when its propeller turns.
explain: Propellers can be dangerous. «Fly a toy drone only where allowed, with an adult, away from people, roads, airports and animals, because propellers can cut.» Never go near a spinning propeller.
fact: A propeller is a set of blades that spin around to push something forward.
fact: Propellers push air or water backwards, so the boat or plane moves forwards.
fact: «Propeller» is a noun. One is a propeller, and more than one are propellers.
fact: «The biggest ship propellers are taller than a house.»
fact: Never go near a spinning propeller of a boat or drone.
exercise: What is a propeller? | A sail that catches the wind | *A set of blades that spin around to push a boat, ship or aircraft forward | A wheel that rolls along the road | A small engine that makes a loud noise
exercise: «A propeller's twisted blades push water backwards as they spin, so the ship moves forward.» What pushes the ship forward? | The wind only | The anchor | The ship's horn | *The water pushed backwards by the blades
exercise: Why should you never go near a spinning propeller? | Because they are very quiet | *Because propellers can cut | Because they keep boats still | Because they are painted bright colours
test: A propeller on a plane pushes which substance backwards so the plane moves forwards? | Water | *Air | Snow | Sand
test: Which is the plural of propeller? | *propellers | propeller's | propellering | propels
exam: Read «The biggest ship propellers are taller than a house.» What does this tell you? | Ship propellers are very small | Houses are made of metal | Ships never use propellers | *Ship propellers can be really huge
